factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 6 problems
  The draft says CBCID investigators are working in Namakkal, but the article says the tip-offs came from both Bhuvanagiri (Cuddalore district) and Namakkal, and the CBCID teams went to those areas. The draft drops Bhuvanagiri as a separate sighting location in the headline, slides and caption, and lists Namakkal as the only location.
  The draft says the girl was seen 'in Namakkal' (slide: 'சிறுமி நாமக்கல்லில் இருப்பதாக போலீசாருக்குத் தகவல்'), which states a stronger claim than the article, which only says she was reportedly seen in Bhuvanagiri and Namakkal areas.
  The draft says 'சிபிசிஐடி அதிகாரிகள் குழு நாமக்கல் வருகை' (CBCID team arrived in Namakkal), a specific arrival claim not stated in the article, which only says the officers have gone to those areas.
  The reel_script says '30-க்கும் மேற்பட்ட போலீஸ் அதிகாரிகள்' and the caption says '30-க்கும் மேற்பட்ட சிபிசிஐடி அதிகாரிகள்'. The article says 30+ police officers, not specifically CBCID officers, so the caption attributes them to CBCID incorrectly.
  The caption says the 30+ CBCID officers 'have been investigating this case for the past 14 days'; the article says CBCID officers have been investigating for 14 days, and the 30+ officers are described separately, so the attribution is blurred.
  The caption says 'போலீசார் தேடுதல் வேட்டையில் ஈடுபட்டுள்ளனர்' in Bhuvanagiri and Namakkal areas and the slide says 'தேடல்' there, but the article says the officers are investigating/going to those areas, not specifically searching for her there.
